    title: "Rubio says 'no imminent threat' to US from Iran",
    summary: "Rubio says 'no imminent threat' to US from Iran US Secretary of State Marco Rubio cast doubt about reports of an \"imminent threat\" from Iran on Washington. Speaking to reporters in the Philippines, Rubio said that US authorities routinely check for potential threats against the country, but added that most intelligence leads are not considered credible. When asked if he was concerned about a possible attack on Washington, he said: \"I am not. But again, we're concerned every day about anything that threatens our country ... I don't think there's any imminent threat.\" \"The United States is always on the lookout for anyone who tries to do harm to our country and to our people. And we have threat streams every day, and the majority of them are not credible. We have to follow up on them,\" Rubio added. Rubio also questioned the credibility of sources cited in a CNN report about an alleged Iranian plot targeting the US capital, saying: \"Some of your intelligence sources are liars; others are liars and criminals.\" \"I won't even comment on it because I don't know who's leaking this stuff to you guys. But they're either showboats and liars, or probably criminals if they're saying anything that's even half true.\"",
    preview: "Rubio says 'no imminent threat' to US from Iran US Secretary of State Marco Rubio cast doubt about reports of an \"imminent threat\" from Iran on Washington. Speaking to reporters in the Philippines, Rubio said that US authorities routinely check for potential threats against the country, but added that most intelligence leads are not considered credible. When asked if he was concerned about a possible attack on Washington, he said: \"I am not. But again, we're concerned every day about anything that threatens our country ...",
    body: "Rubio says 'no imminent threat' to US from Iran US Secretary of State Marco Rubio cast doubt about reports of an \"imminent threat\" from Iran on Washington. Speaking to reporters in the Philippines, Rubio said that US authorities routinely check for potential threats against the country, but added that most intelligence leads are not considered credible. When asked if he was concerned about a possible attack on Washington, he said: \"I am not.\n\nBut again, we're concerned every day about anything that threatens our country ... I don't think there's any imminent threat.\" \"The United States is always on the lookout for anyone who tries to do harm to our country and to our people. And we have threat streams every day, and the majority of them are not credible. We have to follow up on them,\" Rubio added. Rubio also questioned the credibility of sources cited in a CNN report about an alleged Iranian plot targeting the US capital, saying: \"Some of your intelligence sources are liars; others are liars and criminals.\" \"I won't even comment on it because I don't know who's leaking this stuff to you guys.\n\nBut they're either showboats and liars, or probably criminals if they're saying anything that's even half true.\"",
