    title: "News2u Holdings Announces Group Business Restructuring",
    summary: "News2u Holdings Inc. (Headquarters: Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo; President and CEO: Minako Suematsu) today announced that it will implement a group business restructuring, effective January 2027, to enhance the competitiveness and operational efficiency of its media and publishing businesses.",
    preview: "News2u Holdings Inc. (Headquarters: Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo; President and CEO: Minako Suematsu) today announced that it will implement a group business restructuring, effective January 2027, to enhance the competitiveness and operational efficiency of its media and publishing businesses.",
    body: "News2u Holdings Inc. (Headquarters: Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo; President and CEO: Minako Suematsu) today announced that it will implement a group business restructuring, effective January 2027, to enhance the competitiveness and operational efficiency of its media and publishing businesses.\n\nOverview of Business Restructuring (Effective January 2027)\n\n1. Consolidation into The Japan Times, Ltd.\n\n- Transfer of the businesses of “The Japan Times Alpha” and “Alpha J” (currently under The Japan Times Publishing, Ltd.)\n\n- Transfer of the advertising business (currently under The Japan Times Agency, Ltd.)\n\nBy consolidating these key businesses into The Japan Times, the group will strengthen coordination across editorial, sales, and advertising and promote cross-functional media operations.\n\n2. Focus Areas of Group Companies\n\n- The Japan Times Publishing will focus on its language publishing business as well as the rollout of an online Japanese-language learning platform.\n\n- The Japan Times Agency will specialize in its education business, centered on education-related events and educational information platform services.\n\nThrough this restructuring, the News2u Group will optimize its management resources and advance the delivery of high-quality journalism and revenue generation supported by a strong business foundation.\n\nAbout News2u Holdings Inc.\n\nHeadquarters: 6F Ichibancho Daini TG Bldg., 2-2 Ichibancho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo\n\nRepresentative: Minako Suematsu, President and CEO\n\nBusiness Description: Group strategy planning and governance and associated operations; promotion of ESG initiatives\n\nEstablished: March 2001\n\n[Media Contact]\n\nNews2u Holdings Inc.\n\nHuman Resources & General Affairs Department\n\nEmail: [email protected]",
