    body: "Israeli parliament elects Eisenkot ally as speaker in blow for Netanyahu Israeli lawmakers on Tuesday elected Matan Kahana, a parliament speaker from the camp opposed to caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Sixty-six of 120 lawmakers voted in favour of Kahana, an ally of former military chief Gadi Eisenkot, who has until next month to form a government to replace Netanyahu. Netanyahu's Likud party had put forward Ofir Katz as its own candidate, who received 52 votes.\n\nThe parliament speaker is an important office given that it sets the timetable for parliamentary business and can therefore speed up or delay debates or votes on proposed legislation. In this file photo, Matan Kahana arrives for a photo at the President's residence during a ceremony for the new coalition government in Jerusalem, on 14 June 2021 (AFP)",
