    body: "The success of Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi’s economic strategy hinges on investor confidence in the nation’s fiscal health, a key Finance Ministry panel is set to warn as the government prepares next year’s spending plans.\n\n“There’s never been a time when market trust has been more important,” the Fiscal System Council said in a draft proposal obtained Wednesday. Drawing on the example of France and recent societal unrest, the panel warns that Japan is also in a new stage where it needs to be hyper aware of risks stemming from inflation and yield spikes.\n\n“If the government loses that trust, it will struggle to make necessary investments flexibly and consistently.”",
